  "query_preview": "..\nSaturday evening through Sunday: An upper level low will\ncontinue tracking eastward across the region, keeping lapse\nrates steep and allowing widely scattered convective showers to\ncontinue into early Saturday evening bringing brief downpours, \ngusty winds, lightning, and pea-sized hail. Heading into\nSaturday night, the low will shift eastward into Montana, but\nprecip wrapping around the low will keep shower chances in the\nforecast across the Idaho Panhandle through Sunday morning and\nearly afternoon. Across Central and Eastern Washington,\ntemperatures will drop near freezing the next couple of nights \nunder mostly clear skies and light winds, posing a risk for \nmorning frost Sunday and Monday. Those with sensitive plants \nshould take action to protect them from the cold.\n\nMonday through Friday: High pressure builds into the region\nthrough the workweek, driving a steady warming trend.\nAfternoon highs will start out in the mid 60s to low 70s Monday\nand will warm by 2 to 4 degrees each day, climbing into the mid\n70s to low 80s by Friday. Weak shortwaves rippling through the \nbroader flow will bring occasional chances for mountain showers,\nbut conditions will remain dry elsewhere. Overall the weather\npattern is looking rather benign and uneventful through the end\nof the week. /Fewkes",
